  "details": "To my knowledge, the Oculus Lipsync SDK provides each talking viseme with its own float parameter so that one syllable could seamlessly flow into the next one. So I don't see why we can't have that system available to us as avatar parameters, correct me if I'm wrong though.\n\nI basically want to replicate the viseme system with an avatar animator so that I can then modify it in-game (particularly useful for face-tracking). However, the closest I've gotten with the animator parameters (voice float to drive the blendshape amount with a transition time between syllables) didn't reach the same fidelity as the default system. It ended up suffering a transition delay if I spoke too fast or looked stuttery when I spoke slowly.",
